-- title:
--   v-adic valuation as exp of minus the multiplicity of v
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a Dedekind domain, let $K$ be a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure making it a fraction field of $R$, let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of $R$ (a nonzero prime ideal of height one), and let $x \in K$ with $x \neq 0$. The assertion is that the multiplicative $v$-adic valuation $v(x)$ of $x$ on $K$, in the sense of Mathlib's `IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.valuation`, taking values in $\mathbb{Z}$ with a zero adjoined, equals $\exp(-n)$, where $n =$ `FractionalIdeal.count K v (FractionalIdeal.spanSingleton R⁰ x)` is the exponent of $v$ in the factorisation into powers of height-one primes of the principal fractional ideal $xR \subseteq K$ generated by $x$ (here $R⁰$ denotes the monoid of non-zero-divisors of $R$, with respect to which the fractional ideals are formed), and $\exp$ is the embedding of the additive group $\mathbb{Z}$ into the multiplicative monoid $\mathbb{Z}$-with-zero. Thus the two Mathlib descriptions of the order of $x$ at $v$ — through the valuation and through the ideal factorisation — agree, with the normalisation in which a uniformiser has valuation $\exp(-1)$.
--
--   This is the classical identification of the exponential valuation $v_{\mathfrak p}$ on the fraction field of a Dedekind domain with the multiplicity of $\mathfrak p$ in the principal ideal $(x)$, i.e. $(x) = \prod_{\mathfrak p} \mathfrak p^{v_{\mathfrak p}(x)}$. It serves as the bridge allowing orders of zeros and poles to be computed from ideal factorisations; it is used in the treatment of valuations of functions on Weierstrass curves and in an estimate for automorphic forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDedekindDomain_HeightOneSpectrum_valuation_eq_exp_neg_count.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open scoped nonZeroDivisors

theorem IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.valuation_eq_exp_neg_count {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDedekindDomain R] (K : Type*) [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K] (v : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum R) {x : K} (hx : x ≠ 0) : v.valuation K x = WithZero.exp (-FractionalIdeal.count K v (FractionalIdeal.spanSingleton R⁰ x)) := by sorry
